This is a C implementation of the ls(1) command.
Supported options:
-a : Include directory entries whose names begin with a dot (.).
-l : List in long format.
-i : Print the file's file serial number (inode number).

Tested on Linux using standard C libraries (dirent.h, sys/stat.h).
Run 'make' to compile, then run './myls -l -a -i'.